{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/meta/hermes/compare/static_h...cb8a9a3fa39f9165f6db93dcee871cfa625a9753","html_url":"https://github.com/meta/hermes/compare/static_h...cb8a9a3fa39f9165f6db93dcee871cfa625a9753","permalink_url":"https://github.com/meta/hermes/compare/meta:cf2ddd2...meta:cb8a9a3","diff_url":"https://github.com/meta/hermes/compare/static_h...cb8a9a3fa39f9165f6db93dcee871cfa625a9753.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/meta/hermes/compare/static_h...cb8a9a3fa39f9165f6db93dcee871cfa625a9753.patch","base_commit":{"sha":"cf2ddd22324f85e58535dc5b1eaa86d87cf282b8","node_id":"C_kwDOCTDsq9oAKGNmMmRkZDIyMzI0Zjg1ZTU4NTM1ZGM1YjFlYWE4NmQ4N2NmMjgyYjg","commit":{"author":{"name":"Gang Zhao","email":"zhaogang@meta.com","date":"2026-11-12T22:50:48Z"},"committer":{"name":"meta-codesync[bot]","email":"215208954+meta-codesync[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-11-12T22:50:48Z"},"message":"Pass /MP only to the C and C++ compilers (#2314)\n\nSummary:\nPull Request resolved: https://github.com/meta/hermes/pull/2314\n\nWith MSVC and HERMES_MSVC_MP on, its default, the root CMakeLists.txt\nadds /MP with add_definitions(). add_definitions() passes flags that\nare not definitions to every language, ASM_MASM included, so ml64\ngets /MP as well and warns A4018 (\"invalid command-line option :\n/MP\") for each of the three .asm files of boost.context.\n\nAdd /MP with add_compile_options() behind $<COMPILE_LANGUAGE:C,CXX>,\nthe generator expression cmake/modules/Hermes.cmake already uses for\nC++-only flags. C and C++ compiles still get /MP and only the\nassembler stops seeing it. Like add_definitions(), and unlike\nappending to CMAKE_C_FLAGS and CMAKE_CXX_FLAGS, add_compile_options()\nleaves the later try_compile checks alone.\n\nFix https://github.com/meta/hermes/issues/2313\n\nReviewed By: avp\n\nDifferential Revision: D131570561\n\nfbshipit-source-id: 596b2bd030d0ebc9b82fe90a8389cd2c4e72e973","tree":{"sha":"84a7e460bd62df47e1c18e15af08a8c121f1078f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/meta/hermes/git/trees/84a7e460bd62df47e1c18e15af08a8c121f1078f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/meta/hermes/git/commits/cf2ddd22324f85e58535dc5b1eaa86d87cf282b8","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/meta/hermes/commits/cf2ddd22324f85e58535dc5b1eaa86d87cf282b8","html_url":"https://github.com/meta/hermes/commit/cf2ddd22324f85e58535dc5b1eaa86d87cf282b8","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/meta/hermes/commits/cf2ddd22324f85e58535dc5b1eaa86d87cf282b8/comments","author":{"login":"lavenzg","id":22123582,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMTIzNTgy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/22123582?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lavenzg","html_url":"https://github.com/lavenzg","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lavenzg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lavenzg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lavenzg/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lavenzg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lavenzg/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lavenzg/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lavenzg/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lavenzg/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lavenzg/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"meta-codesync[bot]","id":215208954,"node_id":"BOT_kgDODNPT-g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/1373969?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/meta-codesync%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/meta-codesync","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/meta-codesync%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/meta-codesync%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/meta-codesync%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/meta-codesync%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/meta-codesync%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/meta-codesync%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/meta-codesync%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/meta-codesync%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/meta-codesync%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"9cd90277f3e65267a9f0727452019d33150010d7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/meta/hermes/commits/9cd90277f3e65267a9f0727452019d33150010d7","html_url":"https://github.com/meta/hermes/commit/9cd90277f3e65267a9f0727452019d33150010d7"}]},"merge_base_commit":{"sha":"cb8a9a3fa39f9165f6db93dcee871cfa625a9753","node_id":"C_kwDOCTDsq9oAKGNiOGE5YTNmYTM5ZjkxNjVmNmRiOTNkY2VlODcxY2ZhNjI1YTk3NTM","commit":{"author":{"name":"Michael Leon","email":"fbmal7@meta.com","date":"2026-06-12T20:21:45Z"},"committer":{"name":"meta-codesync[bot]","email":"215208954+meta-codesync[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-06-12T20:21:45Z"},"message":"Fix getTypedArrayBuffer bug\n\nSummary:\ngetTypedArrayBuffer() duck-types its argument, reading buffer, byteOffset\nand byteLength as plain JS properties off a caller-supplied object. It then\nreturned {bufferData + byteOffset, byteLength} without ever checking that\nbyteOffset + byteLength fits within the ArrayBuffer. So a crafted plain object\nwith out-of-bounds offset/length produced an OOB read via TextDecoder.decode()\nand an OOB write via TextEncoder.encodeInto().\n\nBounds-check the view against ArrayBuffer.size() and throw appropriately.\n\nReviewed By: avp\n\nDifferential Revision: D108442518\n\nfbshipit-source-id: 0fe741b6817365408cb85acfdd0aa34e6c24b179","tree":{"sha":"3a6d713f8d4